(3984147, 567930, 70888, '<td valign="top">one of these little buggers pulled our 6mo. olds hands/feet out of her crib and proceded to eat her fingertips and toes, tried to at least, blood eveywhere...we had put our daughter to sleep and a friend brought the ferret over and it roamed the house as we visited,we had her(my daughters) door shut but the ferret was able to sqeeze under,oh we heard her cry at first just thought she was being a baby,then softie me had to go get her and found the ferret doing as i described,most people dont realize that ferrets in the wild are predominantly meat-eaters,this particular one had been "in country" only for two weeks pryor to my friend purchasing,even with a "NO RETURN" pet policy he was able to return it and get his money back. sorry for the ramble,nice image 6</td>', 'one of these little buggers pulled our 6mo. olds hands/feet out of her crib and proceded to eat her fingertips and toes, tried to at least, blood eveywhere...we had put our daughter to sleep and a friend brought the ferret over and it roamed the house as we visited,we had her(my daughters) door shut but the ferret was able to sqeeze under,oh we heard her cry at first just thought she was being a baby,then softie me had to go get her and found the ferret doing as i described,most people dont realize that ferrets in the wild are predominantly meat-eaters,this particular one had been "in country" only for two weeks pryor to my friend purchasing,even with a "NO RETURN" pet policy he was able to return it and get his money back. sorry for the ramble,nice image 6', '2007-08-09 14:10:37.000000', NULL, 1),
